===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[reestablishment|re-establishment]] of [[friendly]] [[relation]]s; [[conciliation]], [[rapprochement]].
#: {{synonyms|en|reconcilement|reconciling|q2=noun|saught|q3=Britain, dialectal}}
#: {{antonyms|en|irreconciliation|unreconciliation}}
#: {{ux|en|He longed for '''reconciliation''' with his estranged father, but painful memories made him feel unready to do so.}}
# {{lb|en|accounting}} The [[process#Noun|process]] of [[compare|comparing]] and [[resolve|resolving]] [[apparent]] [[difference]]s between [[set#Noun|sets]] of [[accounting#Noun|accounting]] [[record#Noun|records]], or between accounting records and [[bank#Noun|bank]] [[statements]], [[receipt]]s, etc.
# {{non-gloss definition|Religious senses.}}
## {{lb|en|Christianity}} The [[end#Noun|end]] of [[estrangement]] between a [[human#Noun|human]] and [[God]] as a [[result#Noun|result]] of [[atonement]].
## {{lb|en|Christianity}} The [[reconsecration]] of a [[desecrated#Adjective|desecrated]] [[church#Noun|church]] or other [[holy]] [[site#Noun|site]].
## {{lb|en|Christianity|chiefly|Roman Catholicism}} [[admission|Admission]] of a [[person]] to [[membership]] of the church, or [[readmission]] after the person has previously [[leave#Verb|left]] the church.
## {{lb|en|Roman Catholicism}} {{short for|en|sacrament of reconciliation|t=a [[sacrament]] ([[sacred]] [[ritual]]) formerly called [[confession]], involving [[contrition]] by a person, [[confess]]ing [[sin#Noun|sins]] to a [[priest]], [[penance#Noun|penance]] [[perform]]ed by the person, and [[absolution]] [[grant#Verb|granted]] by the priest}}

